{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And Elohim said, Behold, I have given you, etc.</b> The measure of the verse is as follows: since He had already said ״וּמִלְאוּ אֶת הָאָרֶץ וְכִבְשֻׁהָ וּרְדוּ״ and so forth — by this He made man master and ruler over all creation — and now He comes to state the benefit of the giving, which is for food; and by this He permitted them to eat from the vegetation. And from the implication of the matter you know that what He gave them dominion over — the fish of the sea and the birds of the sky and the beasts — is only to rule over them, not to eat of them, for He specified regarding only one of the subjugated categories that it is for food, and not all of them." "<b>And every tree in which is the fruit of a tree</b>. Here He excluded the Tree of Knowledge, for it does not fall under this category of producing fruit alone, but rather it itself is fruit. And the measure of the verse is as follows: <b>and every tree</b> — and not every tree indiscriminately, but only that in which is the fruit of a tree, and not that which is itself fruit — that being the Tree of Knowledge concerning which he was afterwards explicitly commanded. Or it may mean that even the Tree of Knowledge is included, and although we find that he was commanded concerning it, they of blessed memory already said (Genesis Rabbah 21) that if he had waited until the eve of Sabbath he would have sanctified it over wine up to this point, and from their words you learn that it was not forbidden as a permanent prohibition."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T18:57:37.441781868Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}